{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Devtools provides you with an easy-to-use and modular client that allows you to compose multiple devtools into one easy-to-use panel."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tanstack/svelte-devtools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Devtools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" library. This will install the devtools core as well as provide you with the Svelte-specific adapter."}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm i @tanstack/svelte-devtools","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next, in the root of your application, import the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtools"},{"type":"text","value":" component from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/svelte-devtools"},{"type":"text","value":" and add it to your template."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<main>\n  <!-- Your app content -->\n</main>\n<TanStackDevtools />","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import the desired devtools and provide them to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtools"},{"type":"text","value":" component via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plugins"},{"type":"text","value":" prop along with a label for the menu."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import type { TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/svelte-query-devtools'\n\n  const plugins: TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin[] = [\n    {\n      name: 'Svelte Query',\n      component: SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel,\n    },\n  ]\n</script>\n\n<main>\n  <!-- Your app content -->\n</main>\n<TanStackDevtools {plugins} />","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note: The Svelte adapter uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component"},{"type":"text","value":" (a Svelte component reference) instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render"},{"type":"text","value":" (a JSX element) in plugin definitions. Components receive the shared "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"devtoolsOpen"},{"type":"text","value":" props. Additional values from the plugin's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props"},{"type":"text","value":" field are merged into the same object when the component mounts."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finally, add any additional configuration you desire to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtools"},{"type":"text","value":" component. More information can be found under the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Devtools Configuration"}]},{"type":"text","value":" section."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"setup","text":"Setup","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Devtools provides you with an easy-to-use and modular client that allows you to compose multiple devtools into one easy-to-use panel.\n\n## Setup\n\nInstall the [TanStack Devtools](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tanstack/svelte-devtools) library. This will install the devtools core as well as provide you with the Svelte-specific adapter.\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/svelte-devtools\n```\n\nNext, in the root of your application, import the `TanStackDevtools` component from `@tanstack/svelte-devtools` and add it to your template.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<main>\n  <!-- Your app content -->\n</main>\n<TanStackDevtools />\n```\n\nImport the desired devtools and provide them to the `TanStackDevtools` component via the `plugins` prop along with a label for the menu.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import type { TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/svelte-query-devtools'\n\n  const plugins: TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin[] = [\n    {\n      name: 'Svelte Query',\n      component: SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel,\n    },\n  ]\n</script>\n\n<main>\n  <!-- Your app content -->\n</main>\n<TanStackDevtools {plugins} />\n```\n\n> Note: The Svelte adapter uses `component` (a Svelte component reference) instead of `render` (a JSX element) in plugin definitions. Components receive the shared `theme` and `devtoolsOpen` props. Additional values from the plugin's `props` field are merged into the same object when the component mounts.\n\nFinally, add any additional configuration you desire to the `TanStackDevtools` component. More information can be found under the [TanStack Devtools Configuration](../../configuration) section.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Basic setup\nid: basic-setup\n---\n\nTanStack Devtools provides you with an easy-to-use and modular client that allows you to compose multiple devtools into one easy-to-use panel.\n\n## Setup\n\nInstall the [TanStack Devtools](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tanstack/svelte-devtools) library. This will install the devtools core as well as provide you with the Svelte-specific adapter.\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/svelte-devtools\n```\n\nNext, in the root of your application, import the `TanStackDevtools` component from `@tanstack/svelte-devtools` and add it to your template.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n</script>\n\n<main>\n  <!-- Your app content -->\n</main>\n<TanStackDevtools />\n```\n\nImport the desired devtools and provide them to the `TanStackDevtools` component via the `plugins` prop along with a label for the menu.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import type { TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/svelte-query-devtools'\n\n  const plugins: TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin[] = [\n    {\n      name: 'Svelte Query',\n      component: SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel,\n    },\n  ]\n</script>\n\n<main>\n  <!-- Your app content -->\n</main>\n<TanStackDevtools {plugins} />\n```\n\n> Note: The Svelte adapter uses `component` (a Svelte component reference) instead of `render` (a JSX element) in plugin definitions. Components receive the shared `theme` and `devtoolsOpen` props. Additional values from the plugin's `props` field are merged into the same object when the component mounts.\n\nFinally, add any additional configuration you desire to the `TanStackDevtools` component. More information can be found under the [TanStack Devtools Configuration](../../configuration) section.\n"}
